Digital Graffiti Wall objectives and implementation brief.

## App Goal

Build a production-quality Flutter mobile app for a university project: a real-time collaborative graffiti wall where multiple users can draw on a shared canvas and place stickers over an image-based poster.

## Core Requirements

### Canvas

* Use touch gestures for freehand drawing.
* Render strokes with `CustomPainter`.
* Store each stroke as vector data: points, color, thickness.
* Never store drawings as bitmap images.

### Real-Time Collaboration

* Sync strokes, stickers, and presence in real time.
* Use Firebase services for auth and data sync.
* Send only incremental updates, not full-canvas snapshots.
* Handle multiple users drawing at the same time.

### Stickers

* Support PNG stickers on the canvas.
* Store sticker position, scale, and rotation.
* Persist stickers and sync them across devices.

### User System

* Use anonymous Firebase Auth.
* Assign each user a stable ID and color.
* Distinguish strokes by user.

## Architecture

* Presentation: screens, widgets, toolbar, canvas overlay.
* Domain: drawing state, undo/redo, sticker placement logic.
* Data: Firebase services for auth, Firestore, and presence sync.
* State management: Riverpod.

## UI Requirements

* Main canvas screen with drawing overlay.
* Toolbar with color picker, brush size selector, sticker picker, undo/redo.
* Clean, responsive mobile UI.

## Bonus Features To Keep

* Per-user undo/redo.
* Presence indicators for active collaborators.
* Team/color grouping if needed later.
* Small performance optimizations such as throttling presence updates.

## Delivery Notes

* Keep the code modular and beginner-friendly.
* Add comments only where they clarify non-obvious logic.
* The app should run with Firebase configured on Android/iOS, and should degrade safely when Firebase is unavailable during local development.
* Prefer minimal, safe edits over broad refactors when iterating on this project.
